      AcademyChapter(number: '06', title: 'Global political economy and Pakistan’s external relations', syllabusLink: 'Globalisation, trade, finance, energy, major-power relations and Pakistan’s foreign policy', lessons: [
        AcademyLesson(title: 'Interdependence, major powers and Pakistan’s strategic choices', objectives: 'Connect international economic structures with foreign-policy options and Pakistan’s regional environment.', sections: [
          AcademyLessonSection('1. Global political economy', '''International political economy studies the relationship between political power and economic activity across borders. It examines trade, finance, investment, development, debt, technology and the institutions that govern them. Liberal approaches emphasise gains from exchange and institutional cooperation; mercantilist approaches stress national power and strategic industries; critical approaches examine unequal structures and dependency.

